  "summary": "A distinctive Bosnian embroidery tradition featuring elaborate gold thread work on dark backgrounds, reflecting Ottoman influence.",
  "description": "Zlatovez embroidery is characterized by intricate geometric and floral patterns worked in gold or silver thread on dark blue, black, or red fabric, creating striking contrasts. This tradition developed under Ottoman rule, combining Islamic artistic motifs with local Bosnian craftsmanship, and was historically used for ceremonial garments, religious textiles, and decorative items, particularly in urban centers like Sarajevo and Mostar.",
